.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt RAND_SET_RAND_METHOD 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm RAND_set_rand_method ,
.Nm RAND_get_rand_method ,
.Nm RAND_OpenSSL
.Nd select RAND method
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/rand.h
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 3.0, and can
be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft RAND_METHOD *
.Fo RAND_OpenSSL
.Fa void
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo RAND_set_rand_method
.Fa "const RAND_METHOD *meth"
.Fc
.Ft const RAND_METHOD *
.Fo RAND_get_rand_method
.Fa void
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
All of the functions described on this page are deprecated.
Applications should instead use
.Xr RAND_set_DRBG_type 3 ,
.Xr EVP_RAND 3
and
.Xr EVP_RAND 7 .
.Pp
A
.Vt RAND_METHOD
specifies the functions that OpenSSL uses for random number generation.
.Pp
.Fn RAND_OpenSSL
returns the default
.Vt RAND_METHOD
implementation by OpenSSL. This implementation ensures that the PRNG
state is unique for each thread.
.Pp
If an
.Sy ENGINE
is loaded that provides the RAND API, however, it will be used instead
of the method returned by
.Fn RAND_OpenSSL .
This is deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
.Fn RAND_set_rand_method
makes
.Fa meth
the method for PRNG use.
If an ENGINE was providing the method, it will be released first.
.Pp
.Fn RAND_get_rand_method
returns a pointer to the current
.Vt RAND_METHOD .
.Sh THE RAND_METHOD STRUCTURE
.Bd -literal
 typedef struct rand_meth_st {
     int (*seed)(const void *buf, int num);
     int (*bytes)(unsigned char *buf, int num);
     void (*cleanup)(void);
     int (*add)(const void *buf, int num, double entropy);
     int (*pseudorand)(unsigned char *buf, int num);
     int (*status)(void);
 } RAND_METHOD;
.Ed
The fields point to functions that are used by, in order,
.Xr RAND_seed 3 ,
.Xr RAND_bytes 3 ,
internal RAND cleanup,
.Xr RAND_add 3 ,
.Xr RAND_pseudo_rand 3
and
.Xr RAND_status 3 .
Each pointer may be NULL if the function is not implemented.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn RAND_set_rand_method
returns 1 on success and 0 on failure.
.Fn RAND_get_rand_method
and
.Fn RAND_OpenSSL
return pointers to the respective methods.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_RAND 3 ,
.Xr RAND_set_DRBG_type 3 ,
.Xr RAND_bytes 3 ,
.Xr ENGINE_by_id 3 ,
.Xr EVP_RAND 7 ,
.Xr RAND 7
.Sh HISTORY
All of these functions were deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
